WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.799
To better understand some aspects of MCP,

2
00:00:02.799 --> 00:00:03.900
we are going to start to implement

3
00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:06.440
our own CLI-based chatbot.

4
00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:08.000
This is going to give us a better idea

5
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:11.000
of how clients and servers actually work together.

6
00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:13.279
In this video, I want to do a little bit of project setup

7
00:00:13.279 --> 00:00:14.739
and just help you understand exactly

8
00:00:14.739 --> 00:00:16.000
what we're going to make.

9
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:18.180
I've got a lot of product description over here

10
00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:19.020
of what we're going to build.

11
00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:20.680
We're going to go through all this over time.

12
00:00:20.680 --> 00:00:21.600
For right now, I just want you

13
00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:23.520
to get a high level understanding.

14
00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:27.340
So as I mentioned, it's going to be a CLI-based chatbot.

15
00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:28.760
We're going to allow users to work

16
00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:30.780
with a collection of documents.

17
00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:32.200
These are going to be fake documents.

18
00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:34.180
They're just going to be stored in memory.

19
00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:36.959
We're going to build out a small MCP client

20
00:00:36.959 --> 00:00:40.580
that is going to connect to our own custom MCP server.

21
00:00:40.580 --> 00:00:42.639
For right now, this server is going to have two tools

22
00:00:42.639 --> 00:00:44.119
implemented inside of it.

23
00:00:44.119 --> 00:00:46.659
One tool to read the contents of a document

24
00:00:46.659 --> 00:00:49.919
and one tool to update the contents of a document.

25
00:00:49.919 --> 00:00:52.200
Again, these documents over here on the right-hand side,

26
00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:53.040
they're all fake.

27
00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:55.520
So they are going to be persisted only in memory.

28
00:00:55.520 --> 00:00:56.520
That's it.

29
00:00:56.520 --> 00:00:57.979
Now, before we go any further,

30
00:00:57.979 --> 00:00:59.860
there is a very important note.

31
00:00:59.860 --> 00:01:01.680
Something I really want you to understand

32
00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:03.540
around this entire process.

33
00:01:03.540 --> 00:01:06.379
And that is that on a normal project,

34
00:01:06.379 --> 00:01:09.660
typically we would be implementing either a client

35
00:01:09.660 --> 00:01:11.440
or an MCP server.

36
00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:12.959
So on a real project,

37
00:01:12.959 --> 00:01:15.360
we might be authoring just an MCP server

38
00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:16.379
to distribute to the world

39
00:01:16.379 --> 00:01:18.660
and allow developers to access some service

40
00:01:18.660 --> 00:01:19.500
that we have built up.

41
00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:21.699
Alternatively, we might be building a project

42
00:01:21.699 --> 00:01:25.059
where we make only a MCP client.

43
00:01:25.059 --> 00:01:27.260
And the intent here would be that we would be connecting

44
00:01:27.260 --> 00:01:29.699
to some outside MCP servers

45
00:01:29.699 --> 00:01:32.540
that have already been implemented by some other engineers.

46
00:01:32.540 --> 00:01:33.379
So in this project,

47
00:01:33.379 --> 00:01:36.059
we are making both a client and a server.

48
00:01:36.059 --> 00:01:37.620
And we're just doing that in one project

49
00:01:37.620 --> 00:01:39.019
so you get a better understanding

50
00:01:39.019 --> 00:01:41.620
of how this stuff actually works together.

51
00:01:41.620 --> 00:01:43.900
All right, now that we have this disclaimer out of the way,

52
00:01:43.900 --> 00:01:46.220
let's go through just a little bit of setup.

53
00:01:46.220 --> 00:01:47.260
Attached to this video,

54
00:01:47.260 --> 00:01:50.879
you should find a file named cliproject.zip.

55
00:01:50.879 --> 00:01:53.480
Inside there is some starter code for our project.

56
00:01:53.480 --> 00:01:55.099
Make sure you download that zip file,

57
00:01:55.099 --> 00:01:55.940
extract it,

58
00:01:55.940 --> 00:01:57.660
and then open up your code editor

59
00:01:57.660 --> 00:01:59.860
inside of that project directory.

60
00:01:59.860 --> 00:02:01.300
Just to save a little bit of time,

61
00:02:01.300 --> 00:02:02.459
I have already done so.

62
00:02:02.459 --> 00:02:04.400
So I've already got my code editor open

63
00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:06.339
inside of that small project.

64
00:02:06.339 --> 00:02:07.260
Inside this project,

65
00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:08.380
I would encourage you to take a look

66
00:02:08.380 --> 00:02:10.740
at the readme.md file.

67
00:02:10.740 --> 00:02:12.979
Inside here, I've placed some setup directions.

68
00:02:12.979 --> 00:02:14.419
So it's gonna walk you through the process

69
00:02:14.419 --> 00:02:16.539
of making sure you put your API key

70
00:02:16.539 --> 00:02:19.059
into the .env file inside this project.

71
00:02:19.059 --> 00:02:20.699
And it's also gonna walk you through the process

72
00:02:20.699 --> 00:02:22.139
of installing dependencies,

73
00:02:22.139 --> 00:02:24.639
either with UV or without UV.

74
00:02:25.160 --> 00:02:26.279
Once you have gone through all this setup,

75
00:02:26.279 --> 00:02:28.919
you can then run the starter project right away.

76
00:02:28.919 --> 00:02:31.360
To do so, inside of your terminal,

77
00:02:31.360 --> 00:02:34.160
make sure that you are inside of your project directory.

78
00:02:34.160 --> 00:02:36.080
So I called my project mcp.

79
00:02:36.080 --> 00:02:36.919
And inside there,

80
00:02:36.919 --> 00:02:39.580
I've got all my different project files and folders.

81
00:02:39.580 --> 00:02:40.440
To run the project,

82
00:02:40.440 --> 00:02:43.479
we will run uv run main.py

83
00:02:43.479 --> 00:02:45.440
if you're making use of UV.

84
00:02:45.440 --> 00:02:47.559
If you are not making use of UV,

85
00:02:47.559 --> 00:02:50.839
then it will be just python main.py.

86
00:02:50.839 --> 00:02:52.399
Now I'm making use of UV.

87
00:02:52.399 --> 00:02:55.720
So I'm gonna do a uv run main.py.

88
00:02:55.720 --> 00:02:56.880
And then when I run that,

89
00:02:56.880 --> 00:02:58.800
I should see a chat prompt appear.

90
00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:01.479
And if I ask what's one plus one,

91
00:03:01.479 --> 00:03:03.759
I should see a response rather quickly.

92
00:03:03.759 --> 00:03:05.119
That is it for our setup.

93
00:03:05.119 --> 00:03:06.240
So now we can start to focus

94
00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:09.080
on adding in some new features to this application.